[163.91, "o", "| Mypy errors | 0 | 0 |\r\n"]
[163.97, "o", "| Coverage | 67% | 67% |\r\n"]
[164.03, "o", "| Punchlist items | \u2014 | 8 |\r\n"]
[164.09, "o", "| Resolved | \u2014 | 8 |\r\n"]
[164.15, "o", "| Open | \u2014 | 0 |\r\n"]
[164.21, "o", "| Deferred | \u2014 | 0 |\r\n"]
[164.27, "o", "\r\n"]
[164.33, "o", "**Net new tests:** 3 (empty field, code fence, \\s convention check)\r\n"]
[164.39, "o", "\r\n"]
[164.45, "o", "## Items by Severity\r\n"]
[164.51, "o", "\r\n"]
[164.57, "o", "| Severity | Count | IDs |\r\n"]
[164.63, "o", "|----------|-------|-----|\r\n"]
[164.69, "o", "| MEDIUM | 6 | BH-001, BH-002, BH-003, BH-004, BH-005, BH-006 |\r\n"]
[164.75, "o", "| LOW | 2 | BH-007, BH-008 |\r\n"]
[164.81, "o", "\r\n"]
[164.87, "o", "## Items by Category\r\n"]
[164.93, "o", "\r\n"]
[164.99, "o", "| Category | Count | IDs |\r\n"]
[165.05, "o", "|----------|-------|-----|\r\n"]
[165.11, "o", "| bug/logic | 2 | BH-004, BH-005 |\r\n"]
[165.17, "o", "| design/inconsistency | 4 | BH-001, BH-002, BH-007, BH-008 |\r\n"]
[165.23, "o", "| test/shallow | 1 | BH-003 |\r\n"]
[165.29, "o", "| doc/drift | 1 | BH-006 |\r\n"]
[165.35, "o", "\r\n"]
[165.41, "o", "## Key Fixes\r\n"]
[165.47, "o", "\r\n"]
[165.53, "o", "1. **BH-004 (MEDIUM, bug/logic):** `parse_brief()` field extraction used `\\s*`\r\n"]
[165.59, "o", "   after field markers. When a field had an empty value, `\\s*` consumed the\r\n"]
[165.65, "o", "   newline and `(.*?)` captured the next field's content. Fixed by replacing\r\n"]
[165.71, "o", "   `\\s*` with `[ \\t]*`. Predicted by global pattern library (regex-newline-leak).\r\n"]
[165.77, "o", "\r\n"]
[165.83, "o", "2. **BH-005 (MEDIUM, bug/logic):** `parse_brief()` applied header regex\r\n"]
[165.89, "o", "   directly to content without masking code fences. Pattern headers inside\r\n"]
[165.95, "o", "   code examples were matched as real entries. Fixed by adding\r\n"]
[166.01, "o", "   `mask_code_fences()` before header matching. This is PAT-001 family.\r\n"]
[166.07, "o", "\r\n"]
[166.13, "o", "3. **BH-001 (MEDIUM, design/inconsistency):** `test_readme_metrics_match_actual`\r\n"]
[166.19, "o", "   extracted 9 fields but only asserted on test count. Expanded to validate all\r\n"]
[166.25, "o", "   9 fields (skills, agents, ref docs, examples, scripts, patterns, hooks,\r\n"]
[166.31, "o", "   tests, lines). 4th consecutive audit summary with this recommendation.\r\n"]
[166.37, "o", "\r\n"]
[166.43, "o", "4. **BH-002 (MEDIUM, design/inconsistency):** No CI check for `\\s` convention.\r\n"]
[166.49, "o", "   Added `test_no_backslash_s_in_source_regex` to enforce `[ \\t]` convention.\r\n"]
[166.55, "o", "\r\n"]
[166.61, "o", "5. **BH-006 (MEDIUM, doc/drift):** README \"321 tests across 8,500 lines\" was\r\n"]
[166.67, "o", "   ambiguous. Updated to \"324 tests across 8,600 lines of code\".\r\n"]
[166.73, "o", "\r\n"]
[166.79, "o", "6. **BH-007 (LOW, design/inconsistency):** Hook path matching uses `in` for\r\n"]
[166.85, "o", "   substring checks. Documented as design decision \u2014 Claude Code provides\r\n"]
[166.91, "o", "   absolute or cwd-relative paths, making these path components safe.\r\n"]
[166.97, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.03, "o", "7. **BH-008 (LOW, design/inconsistency):** Stall detection reported \"STALLED\"\r\n"]
[167.09, "o", "   for both flat and growing open item counts. Now reports \"REGRESSING\" when\r\n"]
[167.15, "o", "   items are growing.\r\n"]
[167.21, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.27, "o", "## Adversarial Self-Play Results\r\n"]
[167.33, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.39, "o", "| Classification | Count |\r\n"]
[167.45, "o", "|----------------|-------|\r\n"]
